# Build context for the combined VanFlow image (backend + dashboard).
#
# The context is the PARENT of the two projects, because one image needs both
# sources. That parent also holds unrelated repos and ~GB of build output, so
# this file is deny-by-default: ignore everything, then re-admit only the two
# project directories, then strip their heavy subdirectories.
#
# Named Dockerfile.vanflow.dockerignore so BuildKit picks it up automatically
# from beside the Dockerfile, whatever the context root is — no copying it to
# the parent directory before a build.
#
# Sibling of suite.dockerignore, which also admits ERP/. Every rule below is
# there for the reason recorded in that file — read it before changing one.
*

!cash-van-dashboard/
!cash-van-dashboard-frontend/

# NOTE: no re-admit for the entrypoint. Unlike suite.dockerignore, the Dockerfile
# copies it from cash-van-dashboard/deploy/, which the line above already admits,
# so there is nothing to stage at the context root and nothing to forget.

# Re-admitted above, now strip what must never enter an image: dependencies are
# installed inside the build, and build output is produced there.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.git
**/.gradle
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# Local-only and secret-bearing files. An .env baked into an image is a
# credential shipped to whoever can pull it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.DS_Store
**/.claude
**/*.log

# The image tarballs this repo builds — 100 MB each, and dist-*/ also holds live
# client .env files.
/cash-van-dashboard/dist-*
/cash-van-dashboard-frontend/dist-*

# Runtime data, anchored to the exact directories that hold it. A bare ** glob on
# a common word eventually matches SOURCE — see suite.dockerignore for the three
# directories that happened to.
/cash-van-dashboard/storage
